- install ROS
- install required packages
- configure GPS
```
Step 1: Configure the SimpleRTK3B (Hardware)
The Unicore UM982 chip comes with default settings that might not include the specific NMEA messages ROS needs. You must configure it once using a PC.

Connect the board to a PC via USB (Port labeled POWER+GPS).

Download Unicore UPrecise (official tool) or use a serial terminal (like PuTTY/RealTerm).

Send the following commands to enable 10Hz NMEA output and Heading:

config com1 115200 (Set baud rate, adjust if you prefer 460800)

gngga com1 0.1 (Position data at 10Hz)

gnrmc com1 0.1 (Velocity data at 10Hz)

gphdt com1 0.1 (True Heading data at 10Hz - Crucial for Compass)

saveconfig (Save to permanent memory)

Verify you see lines starting with $GNGGA and $GPHDT in the console.
```

- opt: add serial permissions
```bash
sudo usermod -a -G dialout $USER
```

